SU(2) log-concave square-boundary exact stress audit

COMMAND
make -f Makefile.research probe_su2_log_concave_square_boundary
OMP_NUM_THREADS=<chosen from current RAM and machine load> \
  nice -n 10 ./probe_su2_log_concave_square_boundary 1000000 30

OUTPUT
SU2_LOG_CONCAVE_SQUARE_BOUNDARY samples=1000000 maximum_level=60 checked_currents=17015970 negative_currents=262 log_concave_square_profiles=1000000 log_concave_square_currents=17015970 negative_log_concave_square_currents=262 admissible_insertions=999748 negative_insertions=0 log_concave_cone_insertions=26258 negative_log_concave_cone_boundaries=0 boundary_reduction_failures=0 first_sample=7415 first_radius=2 first_value=-3527082 first_profile_minimum_log_concavity_margin=101 first_square_minimum_log_concavity_margin=0 first_square_log_concave=yes first_profile=[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,47,250,68,13,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0] first_square=[69503,128797,141825,143547,143641,143641,143641,143641,143641,143641,143641,143641,143641,143641,143641,143640,143614,143309,141041,127614,68892] first_insertion_sample=-1 first_insertion_factor=-1 first_insertion_radius=-1 first_insertion_input=[] first_insertion_output=[] first_cone_boundary_sample=-1 first_cone_boundary_factor=-1 first_cone_boundary_radius=-1 first_cone_boundary_input=[] first_cone_boundary_output=[] first_boundary_reduction_sample=-1 first_boundary_reduction_radius=-1 first_boundary_reduction_target=-1 first_boundary_reduction_value=0 first_boundary_reduction_square=[] result=NO_BOUNDARY_INSERTION_FAILURE

METHOD
For each deterministic sample, the audit constructs a nonnegative
integer profile p with interval support by choosing each successive
coefficient within the exact upper bound imposed by log concavity.  It
forms d=p*p by exact finite fusion interval summation and checks every
simple-current boundary

  d_0 d_(K-R)-d_R d_K.

The first displayed failure has minimum internal log-concavity margins
101 for p and 0 for d, so it is an exact counterexample even when both
profiles are log-concave.  This disproves abstract log-concave square
reflection.

For every boundary-admissible input, the audit independently selects a
nontrivial factor Q from the sample identifier, forms p'=N_Q p and
d'=(p')*(p'), and checks every output boundary.  The zero insertion
failure count is bounded evidence for preservation of the
boundary-admissible square cone, not an unbounded proof.

The audit separately filters the generated log-concave profiles by the
complete anchored-current cone, applies the selected N_Q^2, and checks
the output boundary.  Its zero failure count is bounded evidence for
log-concave full-cone-to-boundary transport, not a proof.

For every boundary-admissible log-concave fusion square, the audit also
checks the complete anchored-current cone.  Its zero failure count is
bounded evidence for finite square boundary reduction, not a proof.

All profiles, fusion squares, margins, and currents use exact integer
arithmetic in boost::multiprecision::cpp_int.  OpenMP only partitions
deterministic sample identifiers; the result is independent of the
thread count.

COMPILER FLAGS
g++ -O2 -std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Wconversion \
  -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror -fopenmp \
  probe_su2_log_concave_square_boundary.cpp \
  -o probe_su2_log_concave_square_boundary

